<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Tucapel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1553</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arauco-war">Arauco War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Tucapel was fought in December 1553 in southern Chile, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mapuche">Mapuche</a> forces led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lautaro">Lautaro</a> destroyed a small Spanish column under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-de-valdivia">Pedro de Valdivia</a>, the conqueror and governor of Chile. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valdivia">Valdivia</a> was captured and killed. The defeat opened the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arauco-war">Arauco War</a>, a conflict between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and the Mapuche that lasted for generations.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-tucapel.jpg" alt="Battle of Tucapel" width="320" height="411" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Federico de Madrazo y Kuntz · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pedro_de_Valdivia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
